NAME
    tlsserver - TLS 1.2 echo server demo

SYNOPSIS
    tlsserver [PORT]

DESCRIPTION
    Binds PORT (default 7779), listens and serves one client at a
    time: runs the vlibc TLS handshake (cipher suite
    TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256) through the tls_stream
    callbacks and echoes every byte received straight back until the
    peer closes. The certificate and RSA private key are the fixed
    demo keypair in tlsserver_key.h: self-signed and public, tests
    only, never for real traffic.

    The kernel loopbacks 127.0.0.1, so inside the guest
    'tlsserver 7779' + 'tlsdemo 127.0.0.1 7779' runs the vlibc
    client against the vlibc server with no NIC involved. From the
    host, run.sh forwards guest port 7779 to host loopback 17779, so
    'printf ping\n | openssl s_client -quiet -tls1_2 -cipher
    AES128-GCM-SHA256 -connect 127.0.0.1:17779' drives it over the
    real NIC (slirp hostfwd). accept() waits at most 20 s, the
    handshake 15 s and recv()/send() 5 s per call.

EXIT STATUS
    0 after the listener is closed; 1 on socket/bind/listen or
    keypair failure; 2 on a bad PORT argument.

EXAMPLES
    tlsserver
    tlsserver 9999

SEE ALSO
    ping(1), tlsdemo, echoserver, man hosts
